       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks unsafe, so I need you to confirm it first.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5,100 mg/day**. The usual maximum for immediate-release metformin is **2,550 mg/day**, and for extended-release it's **2,000 mg/day**. This dose is about twice the maximum. At that level, the risk of lactic acidosis and severe stomach side effects goes up.\n\n**What you may have meant:**\n- **Metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum). 1700 mg is a common *daily* total, so it may have ended up in the per-dose field.\n- **Metformin 850 mg by mouth twice daily with meals** (1,700 mg/day total).\n- Something else. Also tell me if this is the extended-release form, since that changes the limit.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away."
