       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this one, even with your confirmation. **5,100 mg/day** is twice the labeled maximum for metformin. I don't know of any clinical situation where that dose is appropriate, and the main risk, lactic acidosis, can be fatal. A confirmation alone isn't enough for me to put an order like this into the system.\n\n**How to go forward:**\n- **If the dose is intentional:** Please enter it yourself or through your pharmacy's override process. That way a pharmacist reviews it and your reasoning is documented. If you share your reasoning with me, I'll pass it along in a note.\n- **If it was a slip,** I can enter one of these now:\n  - **Metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n  - **Metformin 850 mg by mouth twice daily with meals** (1,700 mg/day)\n  - **Metformin 1,000 mg by mouth twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n\nTell me which one you want, or give me another dose that's within range."
